    "scenario": "MPLS TE Bandwidth Reservation and Admission Control",
    "goals": "• OSPF area 0, addressing, Loopback0 interfaces, an MPLS core with LDP and the MPLS traffic engineering baseline are already configured. Every core interface admits {{rsvp_bandwidth}} kbps of RSVP reservations, and {{router1_name}} reaches {{router4_name}} over two equal-cost two-hop paths:\n    through {{router2_name}}: {{link1_cidr}} then {{link2_cidr}}\n    through {{router3_name}}: {{link3_cidr}} then {{link4_cidr}}\n• On {{router1_name}} build two TE tunnels towards {{router4_name}} Loopback0 ({{router4_loopback0_ip}}): Tunnel{{tunnel1_id}} and Tunnel{{tunnel2_id}}. Both must be unnumbered to Loopback0 and must let the headend compute their own path with path-option 10.\n• Each tunnel must reserve {{tunnel_bandwidth}} kbps. Two such reservations do not fit on one core interface, so admission control has to place the two tunnels on different paths.\n• Both tunnels must end up in the up state, and each of {{router2_name}} and {{router3_name}} must carry exactly one of the two LSPs. Do not change the RSVP bandwidth configured on any interface.",
